cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use s1bursts in your research, please cite it as below.
type: software
title: "s1bursts: Sentinel-1 download, processing and compositing in Python"
abstract: >-
  s1bursts makes Sentinel-1 synthetic aperture radar (SAR) data easy to use from
  Python. It searches and downloads the data from the Copernicus Data Space
  Ecosystem (CDSE), processes it with ESA SNAP into backscatter and coherence,
  and composites them on the MGRS grid with local resolution weighting.
authors:
  - given-names: Luis Q.
    family-names: Gentner
    affiliation: University of Zurich
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0006-4453-0881
# The concept DOI resolves to the latest release on Zenodo. `url` holds it too,
# because Great Docs builds its citations from `url` and ignores `doi`.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23918246
url: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23918246
repository-code: https://github.com/lqgentner/s1bursts
license: MIT
keywords:
  - Sentinel-1
  - SAR
  - InSAR
  - coherence
  - backscatter
  - SNAP
  - Copernicus
# Bumped in each release PR; tests/test_citation.py checks them against the
# newest release in CHANGELOG.md.
version: 0.8.0
date-released: 2026-11-03
